<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Freud returns two weeks after intake and is seen by Dr. Vasquez-Lindqvist of maxillofacial prosthodontics on the same day. He finished the varenicline starter week and has taken 1 mg twice daily for a week. He has mild nausea when he takes it before breakfast and vivid dreams, and no change in mood. He now smokes about fourteen cigars a day, from twenty, and says the cigars are less satisfying. He is not yet ready to name a quit date but thinks it may be possible within a month. He has not called the quitline. His pain is unchanged at 6 of 10 on acetaminophen 1,000 mg three times daily. Liquids still leak into his nose at times. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cigars</td><td>About fourteen a day, from twenty</td></tr><tr><td>Varenicline</td><td>1 mg twice daily for one week; mild nausea before breakfast; vivid dreams</td></tr><tr><td>Readiness</td><td>Considering a quit date within a month</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>6 of 10 before today&apos;s reline</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>58.2 kg</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

